    "28": {
      "date": "2026-11-06",
      "edition": "Friday 6 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching staff",
          "heading": "Jake White eyes trusted Springbok ally as Fiji assistant, no name confirmed",
          "body": "Jake White's search for a South African assistant to join his Fiji staff is still open. SA Rugby Magazine reported in mid-October that the head coach was turning to a trusted Bok ally, and recent reports say he is eyeing a Springbok ally for the coaching team. No official announcement of an assistant has appeared, and no name has been confirmed. Fiji meet France in Lyon on Saturday."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Scotland omit top try scorers Darcy Graham, Duhan van der Merwe",
          "body": "South Africa: Springbok Malcolm Marx returns home to Bulls on long-term deal. Argentina lose Santiago Carreras and Thomas Gallo to injury. Kurtley Beale recalled to Wallabies squad at 37."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "SA Rugby Magazine"
      },
      "rung": "storyline"
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-06",
      "edition": "Friday 6 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "World Cup ambition",
          "heading": "Charlie Atkinson says England are aiming for World Cup gold medal",
          "body": "England A fly-half Charlie Atkinson, a Gloucester back with one cap, starts against Argentina in Bath on Friday evening, and he says the squad is chasing the title. \"The feeling is that we're aiming for the gold medal,\" Atkinson says. \"There's no reason not to aim for that trophy.\" That ambition sits against a Six Nations in which England lost four games for the first time in 50 years. England's World Cup pool is Tonga, Zimbabwe and Wales."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Scotland omit top try scorers Darcy Graham, Duhan van der Merwe",
          "body": "South Africa: Springbok Malcolm Marx returns home to Bulls on long-term deal. Argentina lose Santiago Carreras and Thomas Gallo to injury. Kurtley Beale recalled to Wallabies squad at 37."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-06",
      "edition": "Friday 6 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Title race",
          "heading": "France lead north as Springboks head to Paris, AP reports",
          "body": "AP's preview has France as the favourite to reach the Nations Championship final at Twickenham on 29 November, though Scotland, England and Ireland sit alongside them on 2-1 records. The Springboks and New Zealand are the only unbeaten sides, and South Africa lead on points difference. The Springboks visit Paris next week, and AP recalls they beat France there a year ago with 14 men."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Scotland omit top try scorers Darcy Graham, Duhan van der Merwe",
          "body": "South Africa: Springbok Malcolm Marx returns home to Bulls on long-term deal. Argentina lose Santiago Carreras and Thomas Gallo to injury. Kurtley Beale recalled to Wallabies squad at 37."
        }
      ]
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-06",
      "edition": "Friday 6 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Captain's response",
          "heading": "Dan Sheehan dismisses Irish decline talk as 'nonsense' ahead of Argentina",
          "body": "Sheehan has \"full confidence\" in the group and wants Ireland to \"fully back ourselves\" before the Argentina game at the Aviva Stadium. The 28-year-old Leinster hooker is captaining again with Caelan Doris injured, and Ireland sit third in the world rankings despite a string of double-digit losses to South Africa, New Zealand and France. He conceded improvement is needed \"across a lot of areas\", with set-piece the priority: \"Obviously, set-piece is something we need to continue to drive.\""
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Scotland omit top try scorers Darcy Graham, Duhan van der Merwe",
          "body": "South Africa: Springbok Malcolm Marx returns home to Bulls on long-term deal. Argentina lose Santiago Carreras and Thomas Gallo to injury. Kurtley Beale recalled to Wallabies squad at 37."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Aviva Stadium, Dublin"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-11-06",
      "edition": "Friday 6 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coach's game plan",
          "heading": "Quesada says Italy must try to be unpredictable against Rassie Erasmus' Springboks",
          "body": "Ahead of Saturday's Nations Championship match at the Allianz Stadium, Gonzalo Quesada wants Italy to keep the Springboks guessing. At the team announcement he also called Rassie Erasmus the best coach in the world, a compliment from the Italy boss to his South African counterpart before a Test against the reigning world champions. Italy are without a long list of injured players, including captain Michele Lamaro."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Scotland omit top try scorers Darcy Graham, Duhan van der Merwe",
          "body": "South Africa: Springbok Malcolm Marx returns home to Bulls on long-term deal. Argentina lose Santiago Carreras and Thomas Gallo to injury. Kurtley Beale recalled to Wallabies squad at 37."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Allianz Stadium, Turin",
        "referee": "Eoghan Cross"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "Federazione Italiana Rugby"
      }
    },
    "390": {
      "date": "2026-11-06",
      "edition": "Friday 6 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Townsend recalls Huw Jones from injury, picks Kyle Rowe at fullback",
          "body": "Townsend's side for Saturday's clash with New Zealand was named on Thursday, and it is a near-total overhaul: only Gregor Brown and Rory Sutherland survive from the starting XV that beat Fiji in July. Huw Jones comes back from injury to partner captain Sione Tuipulotu in midfield, while Kyle Rowe gets the nod at fullback ahead of Blair Kinghorn. Matt Fagerson returns from a groin problem at blindside, and Darcy Graham and Duhan van der Merwe, Scotland's top two try scorers, miss out on the matchday squad."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "South Africa: Springbok Malcolm Marx returns home to Bulls on long-term deal",
          "body": "Argentina lose Santiago Carreras and Thomas Gallo to injury. Kurtley Beale recalled to Wallabies squad at 37."
        }
      ]
    },
    "391": {
      "date": "2026-11-06",
      "edition": "Friday 6 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Team news",
          "heading": "Louie Hennessey named among Wales replacements for Japan, chasing first home cap",
          "body": "Bath centre Louie Hennessey has been named among Wales's replacements for Saturday's Nations Championship match against Japan, and with it the chance of a first Test cap on home soil. He made his Test debut in Dublin earlier this year. Steve Tandy spoke of \"lots of competition for position within the squad\", and a bench berth for a player still to earn a home cap fits that picture."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Scotland omit top try scorers Darcy Graham, Duhan van der Merwe",
          "body": "South Africa: Springbok Malcolm Marx returns home to Bulls on long-term deal. Argentina lose Santiago Carreras and Thomas Gallo to injury. Kurtley Beale recalled to Wallabies squad at 37."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Principality Stadium, Cardiff"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "WalesOnline"
      }
    },
    "460": {
      "date": "2026-11-06",
      "edition": "Friday 6 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "Santiago Carreras and Thomas Gallo ruled out of Pumas' Ireland test",
          "body": "Full-back Santiago Carreras and prop Thomas Gallo are both out of Friday's Nations Championship meeting with Ireland, unavailable through injury as Felipe Contepomi reshapes the side that drew 28-28 with Australia in September. Number 8 Pablo Matera is one of the few who keep a place from that Test, and Contepomi's stated goal for the three Tests is to be a more polished unit."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Scotland omit top try scorers Darcy Graham, Duhan van der Merwe",
          "body": "South Africa: Springbok Malcolm Marx returns home to Bulls on long-term deal. Kurtley Beale recalled to Wallabies squad at 37."
